From: HandBrake Team
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/qsvenc: honor bottom field first for interlaced
 encoding

The session PicStruct was always top field first, so the runtime kept
encoding top field first even with bottom field first frames. Use the
field order of the codec context.
---
--- a/libavcodec/qsvenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/qsvenc.c
@@ -863,7 +863,8 @@
         // it is important that PicStruct be setup correctly from the
         // start--otherwise, encoding doesn't work and results in a bunch
         // of incompatible video parameter errors
-        q->param.mfx.FrameInfo.PicStruct = MFX_PICSTRUCT_FIELD_TFF;
+        q->param.mfx.FrameInfo.PicStruct = avctx->field_order == AV_FIELD_BB ?
+                                           MFX_PICSTRUCT_FIELD_BFF : MFX_PICSTRUCT_FIELD_TFF;
         // height alignment always must be 32 for interlaced video
         q->height_align = 32;
     } else {
